// A token the lexer refuses in what a file declares, here a parameter's default value, leaves that
// declaration a guess, so the lexer error is reported alone and no semantic diagnostic follows it.
// A refused character is reported once, inside a word as between two tokens, with nothing else.
// @expect-error '\q' is not an escape. In a string, a backslash starts an escape that writes a special character, such as '\n' for a new line, '\t' for a tab or '\\' for a backslash. Write '\\q' for a backslash followed by 'q'.
// @expect-error '§' cannot appear in code outside a string or a comment. Remove it, or move it into a string.
// @expect-error build failed with 4 problems
greet(string name = "a\qb") -> string {
    return name;
}

